            <ArticleTitle>Pyomyositis with toxic shock syndrome presenting as back pain and fever: a case report and literature review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>135-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pyomyositis is an uncommon cause of musculoskeletal pain in children and adolescents living in temperate climates. Toxic shock syndrome is a life-threatening potential complication of pyomyositis. We report a case of acute hematogenous pyomyositis, complicated by toxic shock syndrome, and review the pertinent literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
